theory_blocks.body:
A sketch is NOT drawn to scale and needs no grid or scale on the axes. Marks are awarded for:
- labelled axes and the correct overall SHAPE;
- the coordinates of the points where the curve crosses the axes (INTERCEPTS);
- turning points, when they are asked for or can be found;
- the equations of any ASYMPTOTES (lines that the curve approaches in the relevant limit; a curve may cross a horizontal or oblique asymptote elsewhere);
- smooth curves that behave correctly at the ends (for example not turning back where they should keep going).

